What is Combustion Analysis Services?
Combustion analysis services involve systematic measurement, monitoring, and evaluation of combustion processes in boilers, furnaces, internal‑combustion engines, and incinerators. Service providers assess combustion efficiency, quantify emissions of carbon monoxide (CO), nitrogen oxides (NOx), and particulate matter (PM), and deliver optimization recommendations that enhance fuel utilization while simultaneously reducing pollutant output. The services can be delivered through laboratory‑based testing, on‑site field assessments, or hybrid solutions that combine real‑time data capture with post‑test verification.
